Title: "Spec Operator Aliases"
Id: "f3ca61f3-5eee-45b5-b7cc-5056fd325837"

Text: "Specification capabilities use `:->` for implication and `:<->:` for
equivalence.

```mlg-fragment
capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> x_ member_of X
capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> \\abstract
capability: x_ \"in\" X :<->: x_ member_of X
```

The left-hand side is a specification-like form. The right-hand side is the
fact, builtin target, or specification established when the capability matches.
Multiple conclusions may be separated by semicolons. Reverse inference for
`:<->:` requires all conclusions.

Spec aliases are most often placed in `Requires:` or `Enables:` as capabilities.
A directed capability is how notation such as membership reduces to a type fact
or another specification without also asserting the converse."
Id: "c3b92574-c140-4579-829c-c26f3644276d"
